{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"02ee5d20966a2458b2e4779e49854b721eca883b2387565ee82f70c19b62b4af","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar-mcp server transport and network security","key_entities":["src/rebar/mcp_server.py","src/rebar/_config_schema.py","McpConfig","_SECTIONS['mcp']","TransportSecuritySettings","FastMCP","REBAR_MCP_TRANSPORT","REBAR_MCP_HTTP_HOST","REBAR_MCP_HTTP_PORT","REBAR_MCP_HTTP_PATH","REBAR_MCP_HTTP_ALLOWED_HOSTS","REBAR_MCP_HTTP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS","REBAR_MCP_HTTP_TLS_AT_EDGE","REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED_HTTP","MCP_ENV_VARS","server.json","scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py","scripts/gen_env_registry.py","scripts/check_server_manifest.py","docs/mcp-reference.md","docs/env-vars.md","pyproject.toml","mcp>=1.28.1,<2"],"problem_keywords":["transport","http","authentication","network hardening","dns-rebinding","origin protection","streamable-http","security","mcp"],"propositions":["rebar-mcp currently supports only stdio transport; HTTP transport with network hardening must be added as an optional, configurable alternative to enable authentication in subsequent stories.","The mcp SDK must be pinned to version >=1.28.1,<2 in both pyproject.toml optional-dependencies and dev extras to access the Streamable-HTTP transport and TransportSecuritySettings, and to include the DNS-rebinding fix GHSA-9h52-p55h-vw2f.","McpConfig and the flat coercer architecture must be extended with eight new scalar config keys (transport, http_host, http_port, http_path, http_allowed_hosts, http_allowed_origins, http_tls_at_edge, allow_unauthenticated_http) that derive corresponding REBAR_MCP_* environment variables, with loopback defaults and DNS-rebinding/Origin protection enabled by default.","Non-loopback HTTP binds must require both non-empty allowlists and an explicit TLS-at-edge acknowledgment to start, preventing cleartext bearer token transmission over the network.","HTTP transport with authentication disabled must refuse to start unless explicitly acknowledged via allow_unauthenticated_http, acting as a fail-closed guard until auth is implemented.","Documentation generators scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py and scripts/gen_env_registry.py must be fixed to dynamically iterate MCP_ENV_VARS instead of hardcoding or missing dynamically-derived environment variable names, and docs/mcp-reference.md and docs/env-vars.md must remain in sync with the authoritative MCP_ENV_VARS registry."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785819206040784180,"uuid":"6696e17e-d64e-4561-b07e-f94e4a3bca6b"}